  "generated_model": "[Abstract Model Plan START]\n1.  **Analyze Query:** The user wants to determine the optimal monthly production quantities for each of 141 explicitly listed widgets (Widget1 through Widget141), as well as the amount of CatalystX byproduct to sell, in order to maximize total profit. The model must account for resource constraints (labor hours, Material A, Material B), the generation and sale/disposal of CatalystX (produced only by Widget3), a sales cap and disposal cost for CatalystX, and widget-specific profit and resource consumption.\n2.  **Identify Model Type:** Based on the query, this is a Linear Programming (LP) resource allocation and byproduct management problem.\n3.  **Define Index Sets:** The primary indices are:\n    -   Widgets: \\( i \\in \\{\\text{Widget1}, \\ldots, \\text{Widget141}\\} \\)\n4.  **Define Decision Variables:**\n    -   `x[i]` = Number of units of widget \\( i \\) to produce in the month. Type: GRB.CONTINUOUS (non-negative).\n    -   `s` = Amount (kg) of CatalystX sold in the month. Type: GRB.CONTINUOUS (non-negative).\n    -   `d` = Amount (kg) of CatalystX disposed of in the month. Type: GRB.CONTINUOUS (non-negative).\n5.  **Identify Parameters (from Schema):**\n    -   From product_resources.csv (all rows required, filter: Product in {Widget1,...,Widget141}):\n        -   `LaborHours[i]`: Labor hours required per unit of widget \\( i \\).\n        -   `MaterialA[i]`: Material A required per unit of widget \\( i \\).\n        -   `MaterialB[i]`: Material B required per unit of widget \\( i \\).\n        -   `Profit[i]`: Base profit per unit of widget \\( i \\).\n    -   From resource_limits.csv (all rows required):\n        -   `LaborHoursLimit` = 5,000 hours/month.\n        -   `MaterialALimit` = 24,000 kg/month.\n        -   `MaterialBLimit` = 15,000 kg/month.\n    -   Byproduct parameters (from query description):\n        -   Only Widget3 generates CatalystX: 5 kg per unit of Widget3 produced.\n        -   CatalystX sale price: $300/kg, sales cap: 1,500 kg/month.\n        -   CatalystX disposal cost: $200/kg for any unsold amount.\n6.  **Formulate Objective:** Maximize total profit, which is:\n    -   The sum of (base profit per unit \u00d7 units produced) for all widgets,\n    -   Plus revenue from CatalystX sold ($300 \u00d7 s),\n    -   Minus disposal cost for unsold CatalystX ($200 \u00d7 d).\n    -   That is:  \n        Maximize  \n        \\[\n        \\sum_{i=1}^{141} \\text{Profit}[i] \\cdot x[i] + 300 \\cdot s - 200 \\cdot d\n        \\]\n7.  **Formulate Constraints:**\n    -   Constraint 1 (Labor Hours Limit):  \n        \\[\n        \\sum_{i=1}^{141} \\text{LaborHours}[i] \\cdot x[i] \\leq 5,000\n        \\]\n    -   Constraint 2 (Material A Limit):  \n        \\[\n        \\sum_{i=1}^{141} \\text{MaterialA}[i] \\cdot x[i] \\leq 24,000\n        \\]\n    -   Constraint 3 (Material B Limit):  \n        \\[\n        \\sum_{i=1}^{141} \\text{MaterialB}[i] \\cdot x[i] \\leq 15,000\n        \\]\n    -   Constraint 4 (CatalystX Mass Balance):  \n        \\[\n        5 \\cdot x[\\text{Widget3}] = s + d\n        \\]\n        (All CatalystX generated by Widget3 must be either sold or disposed.)\n    -   Constraint 5 (CatalystX Sales Cap):  \n        \\[\n        s \\leq 1,500\n        \\]\n    -   Constraint 6 (Non-negativity):  \n        \\[\n        x[i] \\geq 0 \\quad \\forall i; \\quad s \\geq 0; \\quad d \\geq 0\n        \\]\n[Abstract Model Plan END]",
